:\"MEDIUM\",\"reason\":\"After free(msg[random_index]), the freed pointer is overwritten by the swap (msg[random_index] = msg[cookie_num-1]). However, if random_index == cookie_num-1 (the last element), the swap writes the same just-freed pointer back into itself, leaving a dangling pointer in msg[]. The index is random (not attacker-controlled), but the freed slot pointer is not NULLed out in all code paths.\"},{\"function\":\"create_cookie\",\"input\":\"message_length (scanf %lld, signed 64-bit)\",\"operation\":\"calloc(message_length, 1) then read(0, buf, message_length)\",\"risk\":\"LOW\",\"reason\":\"message_length is checked <= 0x100 and cookie_num <= 0x1f. calloc with size 0 would return a valid minimal allocation; negative values would fail the <= 0x100 check. Appears bounded.\"}],\"facts\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"Binary is PIE-enabled, 64-bit x86, dynamically linked, not stripped, compiled with GCC 10.2.0\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F002\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"Security: Full RELRO, NX enabled, Stack Canary, PIE enabled, no FORTIFY\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F003\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"libc is Ubuntu GLIBC 2.39-0ubuntu8.8 at /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6\",\"source\":\"RUNTIME\"},{\"id\":\"F004\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"msg array at 0x4060, 32 elements of 8 bytes each (256 bytes total), stores char* heap pointers\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F005\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"msg_size array at 0x4160, 32 elements of 4 bytes each (128 bytes total), stores int allocation sizes\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F006\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"cookie_num at 0x41e8, 8 bytes, stores current count of cookies (initialized to 5 by init)\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F007\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"urandom at 0x41e0, 8 bytes, stores FILE* handle to /dev/urandom opened in init\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F008\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"init() pre-populates msg[0..4] with strdup'd fortune strings and msg_size[0..4] with sizes 0x50,0x30,0x18,0x38,0x40, sets cookie_num=5\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F009\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"create_cookie checks cookie_num <= 0x1f (max 32) and message_length <= 0x100 (max 256), uses calloc(message_length,1) and read(0,buf,message_length)\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F010\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"eat_cookie reads 1 byte from /dev/urandom, computes index = urandom_byte % cookie_num, prints msg[index], frees msg[index], then swap-removes: msg[index]=msg[cookie_num-1], msg_size[index]=msg_size[cookie_num-1], cookie_num--\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F011\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"edit_cookie reads index via scanf(%llu), checks index < cookie_num using JL (signed less-than) at 0x1684, then reads msg_size[index]-1 bytes into msg[index] via read(0, msg[index], msg_size[index]-1). No check for index >= 0.\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F012\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"read_cookie reads index via scanf(%llu), checks index < cookie_num using JL (signed less-than) at 0x17ad, then prints msg[index] via printf('%s', msg[index]). No check for index >= 0.\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F013\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"scanf format for index in edit_cookie and read_cookie is %llu (unsigned long long), but the comparison instruction is JL (signed less-than). A large unsigned value (e.g. 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF = -1 signed) would pass the signed JL check against cookie_num.\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F014\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"msg array (0x4060) and msg_size array (0x4160) are adjacent in BSS with no gap. msg_size starts exactly 256 bytes (0x100) after msg. cookie_num (0x41e8) is 8 bytes after msg_size ends (0x4160+128=0x41e0, urandom at 0x41e0, cookie_num at 0x41e8).\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F015\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"eat_cookie does not NULL out the pointer at msg[cookie_num-1] after the swap-copy. When random_index != cookie_num-1, the old last slot retains a duplicate (non-freed) pointer. When random_index == cookie_num-1, the freed pointer remains in msg[random_index] (dangling).\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F016\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"alarm(60) is called in init, setting a 60-second timeout\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F017\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"Menu interaction confirmed via runtime probe: menu prints 7 lines, choice read via scanf(%lld), create prompts 'How long is the message?' then 'Input your message:', view prompts 'Which cookie?[0-N]:'\",\"source\":\"RUNTIME\"},{\"id\":\"F018\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"description\":\"A negative index in edit_cookie/read_cookie (e.g., -1 = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF as %llu) would compute msg[index] at address 0x4060 + (-1)*8 = 0x4058, which is in .data section (0x4000-0x4010) or .got region. msg_size[index] at 0x4160 + (-1)*4 = 0x415c. Different negative indices reach different BSS/data/GOT locations.\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F019\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"description\":\"The msg array spans 0x4060-0x4160 (256 bytes). Memory below 0x4060 includes: .data (0x4000-0x4010), .got (0x3f58-0x4000), .dynamic (0x3d68-0x3f58). A negative index of -1 to -12 from msg[] reaches into .data and .got regions, potentially allowing read/write of GOT entries or data pointers.\",\"source\":\"ELF\"}],\"uncertainties\":[{\"id\":\"U001\",\"description\":\"Whether ASLR is enabled at runtime (system-level)\",\"reason\":\"Cannot determine from binary alone; depends on kernel configuration\"},{\"id\":\"U002\",\"description\":\"Whether seccomp or other sandbox restrictions are in place\",\"reason\":\"No seccomp-related symbols or prctl calls found in binary, but external sandbox cannot be ruled out\"},{\"id\":\"U003\",\"description\":\"CET (IBT/SHSTK) status\",\"reason\":\"checksec did not report CET flags; binary may or may not have CET support compiled in\"},{\"id\":\"U004\",\"description\":\"Exact heap layout and tcache behavior under glibc 2.39 for the specific allocation sizes used\",\"reason\":\"Requires dynamic analysis with debugger to confirm chunk layout, tcache bin placement, and free-list behavior\"},{\"id\":\"U005\",\"description\":\"Whether the dangling pointer in eat_cookie (when random_index == cookie_num-1) is reliably exploitable\",\"reason\":\"The index is random (urandom_byte % cookie_num); attacker cannot directly control which slot is freed. Exploitability depends on probability and heap state.\"}],\"raw\":{\"elf\":\"ELF64 LSB PIE, x86-64, dynamically linked, interpreter /lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2, BuildID=84dab319bf6fe22134cf0338cbd8071fd8bc06c2, not stripped, source: fortunecookie.c, compiler: GCC 10.2.0 (Debian 10.2.0-16)\",\"sections\":\".text@0x1110(0x891,AX) .rodata@0x2000(0x266,A) .data@0x4000(0x10,WA) .bss@0x4020(0x1d0,WA) .got@0x3f58(0xa8,WA) .plt@0x1020(0xe0,AX) .init_array@0x3d58(0x8,WA) .fini_array@0x3d60(0x8,WA) .eh_frame@0x22e0(0x1e0,A) .eh_frame_hdr@0x2268(0x74,A)\",\"symbols\":\"main@0x187f init@0x1232 create_cookie@0x1399 eat_cookie@0x14e1 edit_cookie@0x1628 read_cookie@0x1751 menu@0x17fd _abort@0x11f5 | globals: msg@0x4060(256B) msg_size@0x4160(128B) cookie_num@0x41e8(8B) urandom@0x41e0(8B) stdout@0x4020 stdin@0x4030 stderr@0x4040\",\"disassembly\":\"init: setvbuf x3, alarm(60), fopen(/dev/urandom), strdup x5 into msg[0..4], msg_size[0..4]={0x50,0x30,0x18,0x38,0x40}, cookie_num=5 | create_cookie: check cookie_num<=0x1f, scanf(%lld) size, check size<=0x100, calloc(size,1), read(0,buf,size), store msg[cookie_num]=buf, msg_size[cookie_num]=size, cookie_num++ | eat_cookie: fread 1B from urandom, idx=byte%cookie_num, printf(%s,msg[idx]), free(msg[idx]), swap msg[idx]=msg[cookie_num-1], msg_size[idx]=msg_size[cookie_num-1], cookie_num-- | edit_cookie: printf Which cookie, scanf(%llu) idx, JL idx<cookie_num (signed, no >=0 check), read(0,msg[idx],msg_size[idx]-1) | read_cookie: scanf(%llu) idx, JL idx<cookie_num (signed, no >=0 check), printf(%s,msg[idx]) | main: init, loop{menu, scanf(%lld) choice, dispatch 1=eat 2=create 3=edit 4=read 5=exit}\"}},\"vulnerability_report\":null,\"primitive_reports\":[],\"target_bug\":\"\",\"bug_reports\":[],\"impact_reports\":[],\"strategy_reports\":[],\"final_exploit_path\":\"\",\"final_report\":{}}",
